# Plugin Development Guidelines

Plugins have two layers: a framework-agnostic **kernel plugin** and an optional **React
plugin** that registers it and renders UI. The step-by-step checklist lives in
[AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) ("Adding a New Plugin / Component"); this rule shows the patterns.
Good templates: [hr](mdc:src/plugins/hr/) (small decorator node),
[collapsible](mdc:src/plugins/collapsible/) (element node with commands, Markdown and
LiteXML), [toc](mdc:src/plugins/toc/) (service + hooks, no node), [list](mdc:src/plugins/list/)
(registry with hotkeys).

## Folder Layout

```text
src/plugins/<name>/
├── index.ts          # Barrel: commands, plugin, React plugin
├── index.mdx         # Docs page
├── command/index.ts  # createCommand + register…Command(editor)
├── node/             # Custom Lexical nodes + $create… / $is… helpers
├── plugin/
│   ├── index.ts      # Kernel plugin class
│   └── registry.ts   # Optional: commands + hotkeys (some plugins name it register.ts)
├── react/            # React<Name>Plugin.tsx, type.ts, style.ts, index.ts(x)
├── service/          # Optional services
├── utils/            # Optional helpers
├── demos/            # Docs demos
└── __tests__/        # Vitest tests
```

## Kernel Plugin

Extend [KernelPlugin](mdc:src/editor-kernel/plugin.ts) and type the class with
`IEditorPluginConstructor` / `IEditorPlugin` from `@/types`:

```typescript
import type { DecoratorNode, LexicalEditor } from 'lexical';

import { KernelPlugin } from '@/editor-kernel/plugin';
import type { IEditorKernel, IEditorPlugin, IEditorPluginConstructor } from '@/types';

import { registerMyCommand } from '../command';
import { MyNode } from '../node/MyNode';

export interface MyPluginOptions {
  decorator?: (node: MyNode, editor: LexicalEditor) => any;
  enableHotkey?: boolean;
  theme?: string;
}

export const MyPlugin: IEditorPluginConstructor<MyPluginOptions> = class
  extends KernelPlugin
  implements IEditorPlugin<MyPluginOptions>
{
  static pluginName = 'MyPlugin';

  constructor(
    protected kernel: IEditorKernel,
    public config?: MyPluginOptions,
  ) {
    super();
    kernel.registerNodes([MyNode]);
    kernel.registerThemes({ myNode: config?.theme || '' });
    // Decorator nodes only
    this.registerDecorator(kernel, MyNode.getType(), (node: DecoratorNode<any>, editor) =>
      config?.decorator ? config.decorator(node as MyNode, editor) : null,
    );
  }

  onInit(editor: LexicalEditor): void {
    // Everything registered here is cleaned up on destroy
    this.register(registerMyCommand(editor));
  }
};
```

- `static pluginName` is PascalCase and ends with `Plugin` (`HRPlugin`, `ListPlugin`,
  `CodeblockPlugin`); it must be unique.
- Wrap every listener / command registration in `this.register(...)`.
- Make `config` `public` when a registry function needs it.

## Commands

```typescript
import { COMMAND_PRIORITY_EDITOR, createCommand, type LexicalEditor } from 'lexical';

export const INSERT_MY_NODE_COMMAND = createCommand<{ value: string }>('INSERT_MY_NODE_COMMAND');

export function registerMyCommand(editor: LexicalEditor) {
  return editor.registerCommand(
    INSERT_MY_NODE_COMMAND,
    (payload) => {
      editor.update(() => {
        // $create… / $insertNodes(...)
      });
      return true;
    },
    COMMAND_PRIORITY_EDITOR,
  );
}
```

## Registry (Commands + Hotkeys)

Plugins with several commands or hotkeys put them in `plugin/registry.ts` (`code`, `link`,
`link-highlight`, `list`) or `plugin/register.ts` (`common`, `mention`, `virtual-block`) and
return one cleanup with `mergeRegister`:

```typescript
import { mergeRegister } from '@lexical/utils';
import type { LexicalEditor } from 'lexical';

import type { IEditorKernel } from '@/types';
import { HotkeyEnum } from '@/types/hotkey';

export interface MyRegistryOptions {
  enableHotkey?: boolean;
}

export function registerMyCommands(
  editor: LexicalEditor,
  kernel: IEditorKernel,
  options?: MyRegistryOptions,
) {
  const { enableHotkey = true } = options || {};

  return mergeRegister(
    editor.registerCommand(MY_COMMAND, handler, COMMAND_PRIORITY_EDITOR),
    kernel.registerHotkey(HotkeyEnum.BulletList, () => editor.dispatchCommand(MY_COMMAND, undefined), {
      enabled: enableHotkey,
      preventDefault: true,
      stopImmediatePropagation: true,
    }),
  );
}

// plugin/index.ts
onInit(editor: LexicalEditor): void {
  this.register(registerMyCommands(editor, this.kernel, { enableHotkey: this.config?.enableHotkey }));
}
```

Keep framework-agnostic logic (commands, hotkeys, update listeners) in the registry; keep UI
state, DOM positioning and floating UI in React. See
[hotkey-standards](mdc:.cursor/rules/hotkey-standards.mdc).

## Markdown

```typescript
import { IMarkdownShortCutService } from '@/plugins/markdown/service/shortcut';

const markdown = this.kernel.requireService(IMarkdownShortCutService);

markdown?.registerMarkdownShortCut({ regExp: /^---$/, replace: (parentNode) => { /* ... */ }, trigger: 'enter', type: 'element' });
markdown?.registerMarkdownWriter(MyNode.getType(), (ctx, node) => {
  if ($isMyNode(node)) ctx.appendLine('...\n\n');
});
markdown?.registerMarkdownReader('thematicBreak', () =>
  INodeHelper.createElementNode(MyNode.getType(), {}),
);
```

`INodeHelper` comes from `@/editor-kernel/inode/helper`. Reference:
[src/plugins/hr/plugin/index.ts](mdc:src/plugins/hr/plugin/index.ts).

## LiteXML

Register a writer and a reader so AI edits (LiteXML commands) and headless export round-trip
the node:

```typescript
import { ILitexmlService } from '@/plugins/litexml';

const litexml = this.kernel.requireService(ILitexmlService);

litexml?.registerXMLWriter(MyNode.getType(), (node, ctx) =>
  $isMyNode(node) ? ctx.createXmlNode('my-node', {}) : false,
);
litexml?.registerXMLReader('my-node', () => INodeHelper.createElementNode(MyNode.getType(), {}));
```

## Upload

```typescript
import { IUploadService } from '@/plugins/upload';

this.kernel
  .requireService(IUploadService)
  ?.registerUpload(async (file: File, from: string, range: Range | null | undefined) => {
    // Insert a node for the file inside editor.update(...)
    return true; // handled; return false / null to let the next handler try
  });
```

Reference: [src/plugins/file/plugin/index.ts](mdc:src/plugins/file/plugin/index.ts).

## Services

```typescript
import { genServiceId } from '@/editor-kernel';
import type { IServiceID } from '@/types';

export interface IMyService {
  doSomething(value: string): void;
}

export const IMyService: IServiceID<IMyService> = genServiceId<IMyService>('MyService');

// In the plugin constructor
kernel.registerService(IMyService, new MyService(kernel));
```

Consumers call `kernel.requireService(IMyService)`. Reference:
[src/plugins/toc/service/i-toc-service.ts](mdc:src/plugins/toc/service/i-toc-service.ts).

## React Plugin

```tsx
'use client';

import { type FC, useLayoutEffect } from 'react';

import { useLexicalComposerContext } from '@/editor-kernel/react/react-context';
import { MarkdownPlugin } from '@/plugins/markdown/plugin';

import { MyPlugin } from '../plugin';
import MyNodeView from './components/MyNodeView';
import type { ReactMyPluginProps } from './type';

const ReactMyPlugin: FC<ReactMyPluginProps> = ({ className, enableHotkey = true }) => {
  const [editor] = useLexicalComposerContext();

  useLayoutEffect(() => {
    editor.registerPlugin(MarkdownPlugin);
    editor.registerPlugin(MyPlugin, {
      decorator: (node, editor) => <MyNodeView className={className} editor={editor} node={node} />,
      enableHotkey,
      theme: className,
    });
  }, []);

  return null;
};

ReactMyPlugin.displayName = 'ReactMyPlugin';

export default ReactMyPlugin;
```

- Props live in `react/type.ts` with JSDoc; styles in `react/style.ts` via `createStaticStyles`
  from `@lobehub/ui`.
- `react/index.ts(x)`: `export { default as ReactMyPlugin } from './ReactMyPlugin';` and
  `export type * from './type';`.
- Users pass options with `Editor.withProps(ReactMyPlugin, { ... })`.

## Wiring It Up

1. `src/plugins/<name>/index.ts` exports the commands, kernel plugin and React plugin.
2. Add `export * from './plugins/<name>';` to [src/index.ts](mdc:src/index.ts).
3. Server-side support: add the kernel plugin to `DEFAULT_HEADLESS_EDITOR_PLUGINS` in
   [src/headless/index.ts](mdc:src/headless/index.ts).
4. Read-only rendering: add the node to `src/renderer/nodes/index.ts` and a renderer in
   `src/renderer/renderers/` registered in `createDefaultRenderers()`.
5. User-facing strings go in [src/locale/index.ts](mdc:src/locale/index.ts); use
   `useTranslation()` from `@/editor-kernel/react/useTranslation` or `kernel.t(...)`.
6. Logging: `createDebugLogger('plugin', '<name>')` (see
   [debug-logging](mdc:.cursor/rules/debug-logging.mdc)).
7. Docs + demo: `index.mdx` and `demos/index.tsx` (see
   [documentation-standards](mdc:.cursor/rules/documentation-standards.mdc)); add user-visible
   plugins to the playground `src/react/Editor/demos/index.tsx`.
8. Tests: Vitest + jsdom in `__tests__/`; cover commands and Markdown / LiteXML round-trips.

## Checks

```bash
pnpm type-check
pnpm lint
pnpm lint:circular
pnpm vitest run src/plugins/<name>
pnpm docs:build   # when docs or demos changed
```
